│ patch_name               │ regime_robust_xgb                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ This rewrite focuses on regime robustness rather than memorizing long-horizon patterns    │
│                          │ that collapse out of sample.                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key changes:                                                                              │
│                          │ - Heavier use of short lookbacks (5–20 bars) and rolling z-scores to reduce regime        │
│                          │ dependence.                                                                               │
│                          │ - Added “market character” trend features such as volatility trend, efficiency trend, and │
│                          │ autocorrelation trend.                                                                    │
│                          │ - Added multiplicative interactions like momentum × volatility regime to help the tree    │
│                          │ model learn conditional behavior.                                                         │
│                          │ - Removed most long-window, brittle absolute-level features and replaced them with        │
│                          │ normalized versions.                                                                      │
│                          │ - Tuned XGBoost to be slightly more expressive than the current model while adding enough │
│                          │ regularization to prevent train-only overfit.                                             │
│                          │ - Kept the feature count safely below 80 and ensured all features use only past data.     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The goal is to improve validation slope and correlation while raising prediction variance │
│                          │ away from the collapsed mean-reverting behavior.                                          │
