│ patch_description        │ This edit targets the train→validation slope collapse by making the feature set more      │
│                          │ regime-invariant and more local in time.                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key ideas:                                                                                │
│                          │ - Shorten several lookbacks so the model relies more on recent micro-regime structure     │
│                          │ instead of long-lived patterns that decay across regime shifts.                           │
│                          │ - Add rolling z-score features for returns, volatility, volume, and ATR so the same       │
│                          │ feature scale means roughly the same thing in low- and high-volatility periods.           │
│                          │ - Add rate-of-change features for volatility, efficiency, and autocorrelation proxies to  │
│                          │ capture whether market character is changing, not just its absolute level.                │
│                          │ - Add a compact momentum × volatility-regime interaction, which often generalizes better  │
│                          │ than raw momentum and volatility separately.                                              │
│                          │ - Tighten XGBoost capacity slightly to reduce regime-specific overfitting: fewer trees,   │
│                          │ smaller depth, stronger child-weight / regularization, and a slightly lower learning      │
│                          │ rate.                                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should help lift validation slope and correlation while keeping the DA gap under     │
│                          │ control.                                                                                  │
