│ patch_name               │ shorter_regime_normalized_features                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ This edit attacks the regime-shift collapse directly by replacing several long-horizon,   │
│                          │ regime-specific signals with shorter-window, rolling-normalized features that are more    │
│                          │ invariant across market volatility states.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key ideas:                                                                                │
│                          │ - Use shorter lookbacks (5–20 bars) for momentum, volatility, volume, and range features  │
│                          │ so the model relies on fresher structure that is less likely to vanish in the validation  │
│                          │ regime.                                                                                   │
│                          │ - Add rolling z-scores for returns, volume, volatility, ATR, and price position to make   │
│                          │ features comparable across low- and high-volatility periods.                              │
│                          │ - Add “rate of change of market character” features such as volatility trend, efficiency  │
│                          │ trend, and autocorrelation trend.                                                         │
│                          │ - Keep a momentum × volatility-regime interaction, but in a simpler form that should      │
│                          │ generalize better.                                                                        │
│                          │ - Tighten XGBoost to reduce overfit-induced slope collapse: shallower trees, more         │
│                          │ conservative learning rate, stronger regularization, and higher min_child_weight.         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should improve val slope and pred_std_ratio while keeping the train/val gap          │
│                          │ controlled.                                                                               │
